        {
          "id": 1505074587,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "In captures having lots of various DHCP clients the endianness setting will need to be continuously adjusted though.\n\nI was also thinking about autodetection per client (based on `dhcp.hw.mac_addr`), requiring some state to be saved. I think it would be possible by comparing the frame timestamp and `secs` field to those of a previous packet by the same client and `xid`.\n\nIn my DHCP captures there are lots of DHCP relays and lots of various DHCP clients behind each relay.",
          "author": {
            "id": 7558431,
            "username": "markkuleinio",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Markku Leiniö",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
