        {
          "id": 1505484639,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "The issue I'm very often faced with is that clients keep asking DHCP info but the servers won't serve them or clients are not happy with the response (for various, usually client side-originated reasons). In those cases the helpful thing would be to have the corrected `secs` value in the column, but autodetecting the cases per client would require state. Currently the shown values are all over the range for the LE clients, which seem to be common enough in the IoT world. I don't see usefulness in per-packet expert infos in these cases.\n\nI added a sample capture above. (Alas, in that case the `dhcp.id` looks like little-endian as well, and its value is increased by 2 with every attempt, so this case wouldn't work with keeping state based on \"mac + xid\")",
          "author": {
            "id": 7558431,
            "username": "markkuleinio",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Markku Leiniö",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/7558431/avatar.png?v=1789663372",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/markkuleinio"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-08-09T05:11:00.311Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-10-01T09:00:22.035Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 241942178,
